<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Dorbyl yr headline shr falls, div up.</title>
<headline>Dorbyl yr headline shr falls, div up.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - headline		387.2	 vs 421.9</p>
<p>    - attrib		  492.0	 vs 439.4</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 165.0	 vs 150.0</p>
<p>Analysts polled by Reuters forecast headline earnings per share rising to between 422.0 and 505.0 cents with consensus at 459.0. They expected the dividend in a 165.0 to 180.0 cent range with consensus at 172.0.  </p>
<p>    Attrib income	   163.78	vs 144.70</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   211.11	vs 222.18</p>
<p>    Tax			 52.04	 vs 73.07</p>
<p>    Interest received     20.61	 vs 16.79</p>
<p>    Turnover		  3,399.37    vs 3,223.75</p>
<p>    Exceptional items     32.05	 vs 4.05</p>
<p>Div payable June 27</p>
<p>on register June 6</p>
<p>Full name: Dorbyl Ltd</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
